{%- doc -%}
  Renders the Mionas mega menu card panel for one parent menu link.

  Shared by the desktop mega menu (blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid) and the mobile drawer
  (snippets/mionas-header-drawer.liquid). `variant: 'drawer'` switches the cards from the
  desktop's stacked layout to horizontal thumbnail rows with a forward caret. Everything
  else - the data, the tagline lookup, the card's anatomy - is common to both.

  NAME MAP TO ../design-system. The theme names these by their slot in the header, the design
  system names them as components, so the two vocabularies do not line up and the token prefixes
  will not match the class you are editing:

    this snippet's .mionas-header-menu-panel  <-  MegaMenu       (--mega-menu-base-*)
    its __card                                <-  MegaMenuItem   (--mega-menu-item-*)
    the top-level bar in the header block     <-  Navbar/NavbarItem (NOT spent - see below)

  Note __item is the <li> and __card is the <a> inside it; MegaMenuItem maps to __card, not to
  __item. The theme deliberately spends no --navbar-item-* or --mega-menu-link-* tokens: the
  top-level bar and the drawer's plain link rows run on Horizon's own --menu-* settings so
  Shopify keeps hosting and preloading the nav faces. Renaming these classes to match the design
  system is not worth it - the block type is referenced by section JSON - so keep this map current
  instead.

  DO NOT RE-DERIVE THE TWO CONTEXTS FROM VIEWPORT WIDTH. The drawer is not width-gated:
  assets/utilities.js sets data-menu-style to 'drawer' when isTouchDevice() is true OR the
  horizontal nav has overflowed. Viewport width is not part of that test, so on a touch
  device the drawer is the live menu at ANY width - 1024px included. An earlier version of
  this doc claimed "the drawer only exists below 750px and the desktop panel only above it,
  so the queries cannot collide". That was false. It is why the drawer variant pins its own
  grid-template-columns in blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid rather than trusting the width
  media queries there.

  The tagline has no equivalent in a Shopify link list, which is why it is read from the
  linked collection rather than from the menu. A link that is not a collection, or a
  collection without the metafield, renders a label-only card on purpose - alignment is held
  by the fixed media height (desktop) or the fixed 56px thumbnail (drawer), never by text
  length.

  Column counts apply to the DESKTOP variant only: 1 below 750px, 3 from 750px, and
  grid_columns_count from 990px. The drawer variant is always a single column.

  @param {object} parent_link - The menu link whose children become cards
  @param {object} [settings] - The rendering block's settings, for the panel_* layout controls
    (panel_max_width, panel_gap, panel_columns). Pass `block.settings`. Omitted values fall back
    to the CSS defaults in blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid, so the snippet still renders
    standalone.
  @param {number} [grid_columns_count] - Columns at >=990px, desktop variant only.
    Overrides settings.panel_columns.
  @param {string} [id] - Optional id for the grid element
  @param {string} [variant] - 'drawer' for the mobile row layout. Omit for desktop.
  @param {string} [labelled_by] - Id of the element naming this group; becomes
    aria-labelledby on the grid. The drawer passes its section heading's id, because that
    heading is not a link and the group would otherwise be unnamed to a screen reader.

  @example
  {% render 'mionas-header-menu-panel', parent_link: link, grid_columns_count: 6 %}
  {% render 'mionas-header-menu-panel', parent_link: link, variant: 'drawer', labelled_by: 'HeaderDrawer-tienda' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_drawer = false
  if variant == 'drawer'
    assign is_drawer = true
  endif

  # The drawer's thumbnail is a fixed 56px square. Asking for a 45vw candidate there makes
  # the browser download several times the pixels it can display.
  assign image_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) 200px, 45vw'
  if is_drawer
    assign image_sizes = '56px'
  endif

  assign columns = grid_columns_count | default: settings.panel_columns | default: 6

  # Each property is emitted ONLY when its setting has a value, so an unset setting falls
  # through to the CSS default rather than writing an empty declaration.
  #
  # TWO PROPERTIES, DOWN FROM SEVEN. The panel paints nothing now - no background, no shadow, no
  # hairline - and takes its padding from the native .menu-list__submenu-inner, so
  # panel_background, panel_shadow, panel_padding_block and panel_padding_inline were removed from
  # the block's schema rather than left as theme-editor controls with nothing to control. See the
  # note in blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid where the panel's own rule used to be.
  #
  # NAMING: every property here is `--mionas-header-menu-panel-<setting id minus its panel_
  # prefix>`, so panel_gap is --mionas-header-menu-panel-gap and the mapping is mechanical in
  # both directions. Some of these used to drop the `panel` segment while background and shadow
  # kept it; they were normalised because the split tracked nothing and made the
  # settings-to-property lookup a guess. Keep new panel properties on this pattern. They are
  # block-local: nothing outside this snippet and blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid declares or
  # reads them, which is what made the rename safe and what keeps it safe to rename again.
  capture panel_style
    echo '--mionas-header-menu-panel-columns: ' | append: columns | append: ';'
    if settings.panel_max_width != blank
      echo '--mionas-header-menu-panel-max-width: ' | append: settings.panel_max_width | append: 'px;'
    endif
    if settings.panel_gap != blank
      echo '--mionas-header-menu-panel-gap: ' | append: settings.panel_gap | append: 'px;'
    endif
  endcapture
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  TWO ELEMENTS, AND THE REASON IS NO LONGER WHAT IT WAS. The outer .mionas-header-menu-panel used
  to be a full-bleed white surface carrying a drop shadow, with __inner centring and capping the
  content so the surface could reach the viewport edges while the grid stayed at 1240px. The panel
  paints NOTHING now - no background, no shadow, no hairline - so the outer element has no rule of
  its own on desktop at all, and the two-element split survives for the drawer's sake only: the
  drawer needs a width on the outer div and needs __inner's 1240px cap and centring switched off.
  Both live in blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid's --drawer rules. If you are tempted to flatten
  these into one div, read that rule first.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="mionas-header-menu-panel{% if is_drawer %} mionas-header-menu-panel--drawer{% endif %}" style="{{ panel_style }}">
 <div class="mionas-header-menu-panel__inner">
  <ul
    class="mionas-header-menu-panel__grid list-unstyled"
    role="list"
    {% if id != blank %}id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}
    {% if labelled_by != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ labelled_by }}"{% endif %}
  >
    {%- for link in parent_link.links -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign tagline = ''
        if link.type == 'collection_link'
          assign tagline = link.object.metafields.mionas.menu_tagline.value
        endif
      -%}
      <li class="mionas-header-menu-panel__item">
        <a class="mionas-header-menu-panel__card" href="{{ link.url }}">
          <span class="mionas-header-menu-panel__media">
            {%- render 'link-featured-image',
              link: link,
              class: 'mionas-header-menu-panel__image',
              sizes: image_sizes
            -%}
          </span>
          {%- comment -%}
            The __text wrapper exists for the drawer's three-column row grid (thumb | text |
            caret): without it, label and tagline are separate grid items and cannot share a
            column. On desktop it has NO gap - label and tagline sit flush, which is what
            MegaMenuItem draws - while the drawer variant re-adds a small one. Both live on
            .mionas-header-menu-panel__text in blocks/mionas-header-menu.liquid; read the comment
            there before changing either.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="mionas-header-menu-panel__text">
            <span class="mionas-header-menu-panel__label">{{ link.title | escape }}</span>
            {%- if tagline != blank -%}
              <span class="mionas-header-menu-panel__tagline">{{ tagline | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          {%- if is_drawer -%}
            <span class="svg-wrapper icon-caret icon-caret--forward mionas-header-menu-panel__caret" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
 </div>
</div>
